  "body": {
    "id": "lem:design-a-fiber-nonempty-criterion",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For a positive selected table \\(p\\), the design-A full fiber is nonempty if and only if\n\\[\nm\\in\\Delta_{\\mathcal E}^{\\circ}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\mathcal C_A(T)\\ne\\varnothing.\n\\]\nThus strict positivity of the supplied margin is an observable compatibility test and not an additional maintained assumption.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "p",
      "m",
      "T",
      "\\mathcal F_A",
      "\\mathcal C_A",
      "E"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "lem:compatible-margin-positivity",
      "lem:cycle-to-scm-lift",
      "def:two-proxy-fiber",
      "def:cycle-fibers"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "If \\(\\mathcal F_A(p,m)\\ne\\varnothing\\), \\(\\mathrm{lem:compatible\\text{-}margin\\text{-}positivity}\\) gives \\(m\\in\\Delta_{\\mathcal E}^{\\circ}\\), and the forward map in \\(\\mathrm{lem:cycle\\text{-}to\\text{-}scm\\text{-}lift}\\) gives a point of \\(\\mathcal C_A(T)\\).  This proves necessity.  Conversely, suppose \\(m\\in\\Delta_{\\mathcal E}^{\\circ}\\) and choose \\((b,a)\\in\\mathcal C_A(T)\\).  The converse construction in \\(\\mathrm{lem:cycle\\text{-}to\\text{-}scm\\text{-}lift}\\), with the positive supplied margin \\(m\\), produces a legal \\(\\vartheta\\in\\mathcal F_A(p,m)\\).  Hence the two displayed conditions are sufficient.",
